<article class="env-corollary" id="602D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/602D">Corollary <span data-tag="602D">3.2.1.15</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a simplicial set, $\calC $ a simplicial category, $\phi : \sCoNerve [S] \rightarrow \calC ^{op}$ a simplicial functor, and $X \in (\mSet )_{/S}$ an object. For every $K \in \mSet $, there is a natural equivalence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  St^{+}_{\phi }(M \times K) \rightarrow St^{+}_{\phi }(M) \boxtimes K \]
</div>
  <p> of functors from $\calC $ to $\mSet $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine the equivalences of Proposition <a href="/tag/D282" data-tag="D282">3.2.1.14</a> (in the case where $S' = \Delta ^0$, $\calC ' = \sCoNerve [S']^{op}$, and $\phi '$ is the identity ) and Proposition <a href="/tag/602D" data-tag="602D">3.2.1.15</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>